{
  "source": "Standard issue plate formats, current and historical, from the Wikipedia article 'Vehicle registration plates of Australia'. In a format, l is any letter from A to Z, d is any digit from 0 to 9, [^C] is any letter except the ones listed (New South Wales plates never start with C, which is the Northern Territory's), and anything else is written as it is. A plate is not locked into a series: every letter and digit that is free in the real format is drawn at random. Only the letters a state's own rules fix (the Y of the ACT, the C of the Northern Territory and the S of South Australia) are written as they are.",
